| Elemental Damage Bonus || Self/Ally ||align="left"|
Increases the damage of weapons and certain abilities. This bonus is multiplicative after damage mods such as {{M|Serration}}, but before elemental mods such as {{M|Hellfire}} (i.e. stacks additively with elemental mods). The elemental bonus will not combine with elements already present on the weapon (e.g. using {{M|Fireball Frenzy}} on a {{D|Cold}} weapon makes it deal both {{D|Cold}}  and {{D|Heat}} damage, and does not combine into {{D|Blast}}). This allows weapons that have modded or innate elemental damage to gain additional damage types that would not be accessible under normal conditions (e.g. using {{M|Shock Trooper}} on a weapon with modded or innate {{D|Radiation}}  will add additional {{D|Electricity}}  damage, instead of combining both elements into pure {{D|Radiation}}).

Some elemental damage bonuses can be applied to [[Companions]], [[Specter]]s, {{A|Mind Control|Mind Controlled}} enemies, {{A|Shadows of the Dead|Shadows}}, {{WF|Saryn}}'s {{A|Molt}}, {{WF|Loki}}'s {{A|Decoy}}, [[Invasion|Invasion allies]] and clones created from {{A|Blade Storm}}. Bonuses cannot be applied to allies suffering from a {{D|Radiation}} proc.

Elemental damage bonuses are granted by:
; Caster and allies
*{{WF|Grendel}}'s {{A|Nourish}} (Nourished Strike buff), adds {{D|Viral}}
*{{M|Energy Field}}, adds {{D|Heat}} (bonus can be applied if allies shoot through shield)
*{{M|Fireball Frenzy}}, adds {{D|Heat}}
*{{M|Freeze Force}}, adds {{D|Cold}}
*{{M|Shock Trooper}}, adds {{D|Electricity}}
*{{M|Smite Infusion}}, adds {{D|Radiation}}
*{{M|Venom Dose}}, adds {{D|Corrosive}}
*{{M|Thermal Transfer}}, adds {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}} or {{D|Blast}}

; Caster only
*{{WF|Wukong}}'s passive (Primal Forces buff)
*{{Weapon|Ack & Brunt}}'s passive, adds the type of damage blocked to boost next attack
*{{Weapon|Dual Toxocyst}}'s passive, adds bonus {{D|Toxin}} to its attacks
*{{Weapon|Lesion}}'s passive, adds bonus {{D|Toxin}} to its attacks
*{{Arcane|Magus Melt}}, adds {{D|Heat}} (Operator amp only)
